# Cloudflare Pages redirects for thesiteoffice.uk (The Site Office's home).
# Format per line: <source> <destination> <status>. Redirects run before
# static files, so a rule here always wins over a file with the same path.
# Pages carries the incoming query string across a redirect; #fragments
# never reach the server, so the browser keeps them itself.
#
# Never add a rule whose source starts with /tracker/ - every approval
# link, invite link and bookmark already in use points there, and the
# app's files stay exactly where they are. tests/frontend/redirects_file
# .test.mjs enforces this.

# Old Site Office template pages -> home page. (v84: the "shop has
# closed" notice itself was removed from the front page - it had done
# its job and the only new entry point there now is "Register your
# interest" - so these just land on the plain home page.) Both the
# pretty URL and the .html form are listed because Pages matches the
# request path before it resolves pretty URLs.
/Rams                     / 301
/Rams.html                / 301
/rams                     / 301
/rams.html                / 301
/cdm                      / 301
/cdm.html                 / 301
/commercial               / 301
/commercial.html          / 301
/contracts                / 301
/contracts.html           / 301
/health-safety            / 301
/health-safety.html       / 301
/hr                       / 301
/hr.html                  / 301
/quality                  / 301
/quality.html             / 301
/site-management          / 301
/site-management.html     / 301
/free-starter-pack        / 301
/free-starter-pack.html   / 301

# Short sign-in addresses. 302 (not 301) so they can change later
# without browsers caching them for good.
/login                    /tracker/login.html 302
/signin                   /tracker/login.html 302
/app                      /tracker/ 302
